{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ושם אלהים אחרים", :translit "v'shem elohim acherim", :gloss "and the name of God, others"} {:he "שלש רגלים", :translit "shlosh regalim", :gloss "three festivals"} {:he "מבזה את המועדות", :translit "mivazeh et ha-mo'adot", :gloss "disgraces the appointed times"} {:he "עובד ע\"א", :translit "oved avodah zarah", :gloss "serves idolatry"} {:he "ע\"א אסורה בהנאה ואוסרת בכל שהוא", :translit "avodah zarah asurah be-hana'ah v'oseseret be-chol she-hu", :gloss "idolatry is forbidden for benefit and renders forbidden in any amount"} {:he "חמץ בפסח אסור בהנאה ואוסר בכל שהוא", :translit "chametz be-Pesach asur be-hana'ah v'oseser be-chol she-hu", :gloss "leaven on Passover is forbidden for benefit and renders forbidden in any amount"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut parshiyot: three festivals (Exod 23:14–17) placed immediately after prohibition of idolatry (Exod 23:13) to equate disrespecting festivals with serving idolatry"} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhut parshiyot: Passover (Exod 23:15) juxtaposed to idolatry (Exod 23:13) to transfer the halakhic stringencies of idolatry to leaven on Passover"}], :frame {:text "The prohibition of deriving benefit from leaven during Passover is taught at Pesachim 21a, and the rule that leaven renders mixtures forbidden in any amount during Passover is stated at Pesachim 29b–30a. The principle that idolatry is forbidden for benefit and forbids mixtures in any amount is codified in tractate Avodah Zarah. The method of deriving laws from the juxtaposition (semikhut) of adjacent passages in the Torah is a recognized hermeneutical technique in talmudic interpretation.", :sources ["Pesachim 21a" "Pesachim 29b" "Pesachim 30a" "Avodah Zarah"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut parshiyot: three festivals (Exod 23:14–17) placed immediately after prohibition of idolatry (Exod 23:13) to equate disrespecting festivals with serving idolatry", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhut parshiyot: Passover (Exod 23:15) juxtaposed to idolatry (Exod 23:13) to transfer the halakhic stringencies of idolatry to leaven on Passover", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:45.785445263Z", :model "glm-5.2"}